WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.700
Image identity matters in production operations.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.920
A tag is a mutable label that points to an image.

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.100
A digest identifies a specific image content set.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.640
Tags are useful for human workflows, but digests are stronger evidence for what actually ran.

5
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:27.080
Labels and metadata can help record source revision, build date, owner, version, service name, repository, support contact, and related release information.

6
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:34.700
They should not include secrets, sensitive internal details, customer data, or build records that reveal protected information.

7
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:40.900
SBOMs help teams understand which packages, libraries, and components are inside the image.

8
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:48.840
They support vulnerability triage, license review, dependency ownership, incident response, and long-term maintenance.

9
00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.820
An SBOM is most useful when it is tied to the exact image that was built and deployed.

10
00:00:54.100 --> 00:01:00.660
Provenance and build metadata can support supply-chain review when produced and protected appropriately.

11
00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:07.640
They can help answer where the image came from, which source revision produced it, which build system built it, and which process approved it.

12
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:14.240
Image promotion should make it clear which artifact was built, tested, approved, and deployed.

13
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:20.020
Rebuilding from the same source is not always the same as promoting the same artifact.

14
00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:24.280
Clear promotion rules reduce ambiguity during release and rollback.

15
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.880
Stale tags, ambiguous latest tags, and undocumented rebuilds make incident response harder.

16
00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:41.620
When a production issue appears, teams need to identify the exact image content, dependencies, base image, build inputs, and approval path quickly.
